**Important:** The guidelines require the code, experiment evidence and necessary model artifacts in the public repository. We should not blindly ignore all models/results. Later we'll selectively commit the required artifacts, logs and results. Also, don't put evaluator ground-truth route files into your UI or prediction pipeline.

# Step 6 — Create the initial README

Your README is the first thing evaluators and teammates see when they open GitHub. Start with this version.

<WritingBlock id="58321" variant="document"># PathSnap 🗺️

**Distributed ML-based GPS Map Matching & Route Reconstruction**

PathSnap reconstructs realistic vehicle routes by matching noisy GPS observations to a road network using machine learning and sequence-based decoding.

## Project Overview

GPS observations can be inaccurate due to noise, signal interference, urban environments, and missing observations. PathSnap aims to identify the most likely road segments and reconstruct a realistic continuous vehicle route.

## System Architecture

- Data processing and preprocessing
- Candidate road generation
- Feature engineering
- Machine learning model training and comparison
- Bayesian hyperparameter optimization
- HMM-based sequence modeling
- Viterbi route decoding
- FastAPI backend
- Evaluator-facing UI
- Geographic route visualization

## Repository Structure

- `src/` — Core processing, features, models, decoder, evaluation and visualization
- `backend/` — FastAPI application
- `frontend/` — Evaluator UI
- `configs/` — Configuration files
- `experiments/` — Experiments and training records
- `artifacts/` — Trained models and supporting artifacts
- `results/` — Metrics, graphs and route visualizations
- `tests/` — Unit and integration tests
- `docs/` — Project documentation

## Setup

Setup instructions will be updated as the project dependencies and deployment environment are finalized.

## Running the System

Instructions for starting the backend and UI will be added after integration.

## Team

PathSnap is developed as part of the UE24CS352A Machine Learning course at PES University.</WritingBlock>

We'll update this as the project actually works. Don't claim completed model results or implementation details in README until they're real.

